# Node documentation

- These Markdown files are user-facing node help, embedded by the catalog.
  Keep Chinese and English versions equivalent and register both in the existing
  documentation mapping. Short catalog descriptions are not a substitute.
- Describe the actual node input, parameter defaults/ranges, preprocessing,
  output fields and limitations after checking Catalog, Kernel, Runtime and SCI.
- Keep help focused on using and interpreting the node. For each test or
  selectable variant, retain its null and alternative hypotheses, core statistic
  formula, reference distribution/degrees of freedom and result interpretation.
- Define necessary symbols briefly beside the formula. Omit standalone notation,
  sample-moment tutorials, derivations, elementary worked examples and internal
  numerical branches. Link to references for detailed mathematics.
- Retain only conditions and conventions that affect node use or interpretation,
  such as sample requirements, weighting, kurtosis convention and output indexing.
  Do not invent tests or p-values for descriptive diagnostics or decompositions.
- Avoid repetitive generic caveats, exhaustive failure lists and reference
  sections for their own sake. Add an example only when it clarifies an actual
  parameter, expression syntax or output-indexing ambiguity.
- Use `$...$` and `$$...$$` math supported by the existing Markdown renderer;
  verify changed formulas render. Keep maintenance rules and backend paths out
  of user-facing prose.
